<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The widget drawn on a surface this app put there — its own panel, or the tinted
  scrim. No text shadow, because there is no photo under the text to separate it from;
  for the one backdrop that has one see widget_timer_wallpaper.xml.

  Text colours come from the -night resource pair, which is right for the panel: the
  text and the card behind it are the same qualifier's answer, so they cannot disagree.
  A scrim overrides all four at draw time and has to — it is translucent, so the
  wallpaper still has a say in which tone reads on it, and that is a question no
  qualifier can answer. Same for the background: the panel takes the drawable declared
  below, a scrim replaces it. See WidgetRenderer.layoutFor, and WidgetScrimTest, which
  pins the overrides this file's defaults would otherwise show through.

  One layout serves every size: the launcher is handed a RemoteViews per entry of a
  size map built from this file — different rows hidden, and the padding and label
  sizes overridden per entry — and picks whichever best fits the cell. The sizes
  declared here are what a cell with room for everything gets; see
  WidgetRenderer.variantFor, which decides that from the cell rather than from a
  table of them.

  The root is @android:id/background rather than an id of our own, and it has to be:
  a launcher rounds the corners of the widget's background view, and that id is the
  only way it can be told which view that is. Told nothing, Launcher3 guesses — it
  walks down from the root through views that draw nothing, stops at the first that
  does, and rounds *that*, taking the whole widget with it. A variant showing one row
  is a chain of exactly that shape, so the guess lands on the row of text and the
  launcher clips the widget to a rounded box the height of one line. See
  WidgetRoundingTest, which pins the rule this satisfies.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@android:id/background"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:padding="@dimen/widget_padding">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_name"
        style="@style/WidgetName"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_secondary" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_value"
        style="@style/WidgetValue"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary" />

    <Chronometer
        android:id="@+id/widget_ticker"
        style="@style/WidgetValue.Ticking"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:visibility="gone" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_footer"
        style="@style/WidgetFooter"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_secondary" />
</LinearLayout>
